        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve ANSI sanitizer state across bash chunks",
        "body": "Closes #103668\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running bash commands through agents could see ANSI/OSC control-sequence fragments leak into streamed tool output, final bash results, and full-output spill files when a process split a terminal sequence across output callbacks.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix adds a reusable incremental ANSI sequence stripper in terminal-core and lets the bash output accumulator use one sanitizer instance for the lifetime of each command. This preserves streaming and bounded-memory behavior while keeping one-shot `stripAnsiSequences()` semantics unchanged for existing callers.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBash output sanitization is now invariant to callback chunking for OSC and CSI sequences. Agents and users receive the same clean output whether the process emits a complete sequence in one callback or splits it across callbacks.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore this patch, sanitizing `A\\x1b]0;title` and `\\x07B` independently leaked fragments such as `Aitle\\x07B`; whole-input sanitization returned `AB`.\n\nFocused regression proof on this branch:\n\n```text\n$ PATH=\"/Users/xjch/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin:$PATH\" node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/terminal-core/src/ansi.test.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/output-accumulator.test.ts src/agents/sessions/bash-executor.test.ts\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.unit-fast.config.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  22 passed (22)\n\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n\n[test] passed 2 Vitest shards in 12.60s\n```\n\nAdditional validation:\n\n```text\n$ PATH=\"/Users/xjch/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin:$PATH\" node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs packages/terminal-core/src/ansi.ts packages/terminal-core/src/ansi.test.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/output-accumulator.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/output-accumulator.test.ts src/agents/sessions/bash-executor.ts src/agents/sessions/bash-executor.test.ts\n# passed\n\n$ git diff --check\n# passed\n```\n\nThe new tests cover:\n\n- terminal-core incremental stripping for split ESC OSC, C1 OSC, ESC CSI, and C1 CSI sequences;\n- `OutputAccumulator.finish()` flushing stateful transforms;\n- the real `executeBashWithOperations()` path proving streamed chunks and final output are `ABCDEFGH` for split ANSI/OSC chunks;\n- spilled full-output files preserving the sanitized `AB\\n` output when split OSC data exceeds the truncation threshold.\n",
        "branch": "fix/103668-stateful-ansi-sanitizer",
